\subsection{Rastislav Draho\v{s}'s independent replication and control-graph verification}

Rastislav Draho\v{s} used independent code to carry out a complete replication of the fractal-graph quantum system. He re-ran the original script and obtained exactly the same Li-Draho\v{s}-Sultanov Valley on the $2^{15}$ Hilbert space, confirming that the valley is completely consistent under different eigensolver seeds and after averaging over the entire degenerate ground-state manifold. He also ran control experiments on ring, random, and tree graphs, revealing that the anomalous depth of the LDS Valley is about $1.8$ times that of the ring graph and $2.6$ times that of the random graph, suggesting that the topology of the relation graph determines not only the presence or absence of Silent Discordance, but also its quantitative strength.

\subsection{Critical effect of the contradiction-edge position}

After changing the contradiction-edge position from $(0,2)$ to $(0,1)$, the Li-Draho\v{s}-Sultanov Valley completely disappeared. This discovery reveals the decisive role of the injection point of the driving force.

